#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 780.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134608} :activity/id #uuid "25739194-82c1-5788-9ee1-b6fee61cbd79" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049399 :topic/id #uuid "f1aa8ae2-23cf-5d91-8af0-a43e9db5e668" :topic/math-academy-id 2214} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134608 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135191 :tutorial/content "The explicit formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence is\n\n$$\na_n = a_1 + (n-1)d, \\quad n \\geq 1.\n$$\n\nEvery arithmetic sequence can also be written using the following recursive formula:\n\n![](images/a2/a2d28772cb4cb6078d2fccdca054ec1c2dccf27a5ea0b5972b9ac174eaad671f.svg)\n\nFor example, suppose that we're given the following explicit formula for an arithmetic sequence:\n\n$$\na_n =2n+6, \\quad n\\geq 1\n$$\n\nTo convert to a recursive formula, we just need to work out the first term and common difference. The first two terms are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =2(1)+6=8 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =2(2)+6=10,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the common difference is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =10-8 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first term is $a_1={\\color{blue}8}$ and the common difference is $d={\\color{red}2}.$ Therefore, the recursive formula is as follows:\n\n$$\na_{n+1} = a_n + {\\color{red}2}, \\quad a_1 = {\\color{blue}8}, \\quad n \\geq 1\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "b6cd14c7-922b-5e05-9c8e-b842717155ad" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8910 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "02ae2395-79da-5dc3-9f17-a75936abdc07" :step/math-academy-id 191930 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134609}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134609 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133746 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133531 :question/id #uuid "00113d76-b950-513e-a3ea-29eef91c9cec" :question/math-academy-id "e-14383"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b8b10a8-f81a-5dae-b54e-b10959e3ad14" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050157} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050380}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134163} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134446} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560987} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561011}] :knowledge-point/title "Converting an Explicit Formula to a Recursive Formula"} :step/id #uuid "ed82570d-8cc5-564d-8da6-d86c3395fced" :step/math-academy-id 191931 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134610}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134610 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133747 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133532 :question/id #uuid "e04ad3e0-888e-51c0-b60c-e816b7df514b" :question/math-academy-id "e-14386"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d36a3a61-e23b-5ce3-ac65-f7ac1691ec4e" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134177} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134447} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560975} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561005} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573929}] :knowledge-point/title "Converting an Explicit Formula to a Recursive Formula Using Function Notation"} :step/id #uuid "340d50dc-babe-5074-be5e-52e39f437e88" :step/math-academy-id 191934 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134611}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134611 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135192 :tutorial/content "It's often more useful to translate from the recursive formula to an explicit one. So how do we find the explicit formula for the arithmetic sequence defined recursively as\n\n$$\na_{n+1} = a_n + {\\color{red}1},\\, \\quad a_1 = {\\color{blue}6},\\, \\quad n\\geq 1?\n$$\n\nThe explicit formula is\n\n$$\na_n = a_1 + (n-1)d, \\quad n \\geq 1,\n$$\n\nso we just need to determine the first term $a_1$ and the common difference $d.$\n\nWe are given that the first term is $a_1={\\color{blue}6},$ and we can use the recursive rule to compute the second term, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & ={a}_{1}+1 \\\\  & =6+1 \\\\  & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the first and second terms, we can compute the common difference:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =7-6 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $a_1 = {\\color{blue}6}$ and $d={\\color{red}1}$ into the formula for the $n$th term:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\na_n&= a_{1}+(n-1)d \\[3pt]\n&= {\\color{blue}6} + (n - 1)({\\color{red}1}) \\[3pt]\n& =6 + n-1\\[3pt]\n&=n+5\n}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the formula for the $n$th term is\n\n$$\na_n=n+5, \\quad n \\geq 1.\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "c6c5b9f8-4c71-5c1f-8841-3f22646e5074" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8914 :tutorial/title "Translating From the Recursive to the Explicit Formula"} :step/id #uuid "7cd53e1d-4c0c-570b-bef4-68f8081c2fef" :step/math-academy-id 191938 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134612}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134612 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133748 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133533 :question/id #uuid "d732cfb5-9db5-535d-adb1-5d3292f1c497" :question/math-academy-id "e-14389"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "36e1e439-ec4a-5577-80d5-3b113bf36e74" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134056} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134164} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233564} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233571} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233578} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560995} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561033} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563761} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573867}] :knowledge-point/title "Converting a Recursive Formula to an Explicit Formula"} :step/id #uuid "2a238f59-a780-5248-bfa5-a217bec91d6c" :step/math-academy-id 191939 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134613}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134613 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133749 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133534 :question/id #uuid "26b3b89d-d485-51ac-b964-8377ce3aff28" :question/math-academy-id "e-14393"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "baac268a-629e-5887-885a-49393c72776f" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134178} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134479} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560974} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561053} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573892}] :knowledge-point/title "Converting a Recursive Formula to an Explicit Formula Using Function Notation"} :step/id #uuid "c81f0b63-4b36-56b0-bc0f-1535d35453ef" :step/math-academy-id 191943}] :activity/title "Translating Between Explicit and Recursive Formulas for Arithmetic Sequences" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186134049}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046647} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573964} :activity/id #uuid "e9ac0cb4-6981-5a23-a13c-931e769c0a5f" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049399 :topic/id #uuid "f1aa8ae2-23cf-5d91-8af0-a43e9db5e668" :topic/math-academy-id 2214} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573957 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573929 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "550f77dc-9e9b-5195-9763-7cdb0bd797a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "f(n+1)=f(n)+3,\\,f(1)=3,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573529} {:answer/id #uuid "6dd09cb9-9915-5235-adc4-06fee0606cb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "f(n+1)=f(n)+2,\\,f(1)=2,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573557} {:answer/id #uuid "8eac6900-fa95-521d-8075-10f933d001d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "f(n+1)=f(n)+3,\\,f(1)=1,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573606} {:answer/id #uuid "e65964ba-5289-5d29-a387-4942aedcf86d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "f(n+1)=f(n)+2,\\,f(1)=3,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573728} {:answer/id #uuid "ef279d49-69f7-5367-a2f4-b0872ff0863a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "f(n+1)=f(n)+2,\\,f(1)=1,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573741}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573741} :answer-field/id #uuid "583de106-1da8-55aa-9af5-406d2cd33e11" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573806}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d00ab483-f4c8-5391-8669-509347c93245" :question/math-academy-id "q-45073" :question/problem "The formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence is $f(n)=2n-1$ for $n\\ge 1.$  What is the recursive formula for this sequence?" :question/worked-solution "The recursive formula for an arithmetic sequence is as follows:\n\n$$\nf(n+1)=f(n)+d,\\,f(1)=___\\,,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$\n\nTo complete the formula, we need to work out the first term and common difference. The first two terms are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) & =2(1)-1=1 \\\\ f(2) & =2(2)-1=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the common difference is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =f(2)-f(1) \\\\  & =3-1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first term is $f(1)=1$ and the common difference is $d=2.$ Therefore, the recursive formula is as follows:\n\n$$\nf(n+1)=f(n)+2,\\,f(1)=1,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "38039d07-5dd2-5b6c-a30f-ba7e4fa4d943" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573958}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573958 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573867 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22fa8818-c1f0-546b-8129-04f0f8efe572" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "11-6n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573465}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573465} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a4f5b21-deab-56d0-89a1-a958bfd20469" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573830}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0567f346-23f3-5836-b41f-674f2f72a9b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-236727" :question/problem "Consider the following arithmetic sequence:\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}-6,\\,\\,{a}_{1}=5,\\,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$\n\nThe explicit formula for the $n$th term is\n\n${a}_{n}=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,n\\ge 1.$" :question/worked-solution "The explicit formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}+(n-1)d,\\,n\\ge 1,\n$$\n\nso we need to determine the first term ${a}_{1}$ and the common difference $d.$\n\nWe are given that the first term is ${a}_{1}=5,$ and we can use the recursive rule to compute the second term, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & ={a}_{1}-6 \\\\  & =5-6 \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the first and second terms, we can compute the common difference:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =-1-5 \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute ${a}_{1}=5$ and $d=-6$ into the formula for the $n$th term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =5+(n-1)(-6) \\\\  & =5-6n+6 \\\\  & =11-6n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the formula for the $n$th term is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=11-6n,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "44b6d9d9-623a-5d23-8b96-07222f1c044f"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573964 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573892 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f9f2fc8-badb-5594-8c3a-ed2a49aecc2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "f(n)=-\\frac{3}{2}n+\\frac{1}{2},\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573483} {:answer/id #uuid "aa08630a-8958-53e1-8c29-46cc5544822a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "f(n)=-\\frac{3}{2}n+2,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573645} {:answer/id #uuid "c98e8541-844d-564c-9d52-b70e2eab69ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "f(n)=-\\frac{3}{4}n-\\frac{3}{2},\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573688} {:answer/id #uuid "d416384f-a3cd-5fbf-8588-a55b76de1f09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "f(n)=-\\frac{3}{4}n-2,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573704} {:answer/id #uuid "d939c8f0-f058-53f1-8e21-649440c7b894" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "f(n)=-\\frac{3}{4}n-\\frac{1}{2},\\,n\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573711}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573711} :answer-field/id #uuid "cdc27b07-45b8-5bb2-9278-1c5be0b7fdfb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573846}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "69a646b1-c870-5cd4-b54f-601f21d9c0db" :question/math-academy-id "q-45064" :question/problem "What is the explicit formula for the $n$th term of the sequence\n\n$$\nf(n+1)=f(n)-\\frac{3}{4},\\,\\,f(1)=-\\frac{5}{4},\\,\\,n\\ge 1?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The explicit formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence (in function notation) is\n\n$$\nf(n)=f(1)+(n-1)d,\\,n\\ge 1,\n$$\n\nso we need to determine the first term $f(1)$ and the common difference $d.$\n\nWe are given that the first term is $f(1)=-\\frac{5}{4},$ and we can use the recursive rule to compute the second term, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2) & =f(1)-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{4}-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the first and second terms, we can compute the common difference:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =f(2)-f(1) \\\\  & =-2-(-\\frac{5}{4}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $f(1)=-\\frac{5}{4}$ and $d=-\\frac{3}{4}$ into the formula for the $n$th term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(n) & =f(1)+(n-1)d \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{4}+(n-1)(-\\frac{3}{4}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{4}-\\frac{3}{4}n+\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}n-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the formula for the $n$th term is\n\n$$\nf(n)=-\\frac{3}{4}n-\\frac{1}{2},\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "6d84467b-50a1-57ce-a046-4f186131de9b" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573957}}] :activity/title "Translating Between Explicit and Recursive Formulas for Arithmetic Sequences" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573420}]}
